{
  "_notes": [
    "targets: FQCNs whose params get rewritten to the types in 'rewrite'. Enum FQCNs are allowed (detected via PsiClass.isEnum()).",
    "wrappers: FQCNs unwrapped recursively (first type argument) until a non-wrapper type is found, e.g. Holder<ItemStack> -> ItemStack. If unwrapping fails (raw type, unresolvable class), the param is left as-is.",
    "Holder / HolderSet / Holder.Reference are known future wrappers; add them here when ready, no code change needed.",
    "typeRules: per-generic-type rules, evaluated recursively inside-out, so nesting like List<Holder<ItemStack>> resolves to List<Object>.",
    "  action=keep: keep the outer type, recursively rewrite the listed type-argument indices (0-based). e.g. Map<String, ItemStack> -> Map<String, Object>; List<String> stays untouched.",
    "  action=replace: rebuild the type as 'replaceWith' with the listed args rewritten. If 'requireEligibleArg' is set (index), the rule only fires when that arg resolves (through wrappers) to a target. e.g. HolderSet<ItemStack> -> List<Object>; HolderSet<String> stays untouched.",
    "rewrite: replacement types for direct target hits per param shape. scalar = plain param, array = varargs/array param, collection = Collection/List/Set param with no specific typeRule.",
    "enumsToObject: when true, any param resolving to an enum (PsiClass.isEnum) rewrites to the scalar type without listing it, including type variables bounded by Enum/an enum (covers Enum.compareTo(E)). Widens the prefilter since enum-ness needs resolve().",
    "This file is reloaded automatically when modified; a broken file keeps serving the last good config."
  ],
  "targets": [
    "com.google.gson.JsonArray",
    "com.google.gson.JsonElement",
    "com.google.gson.JsonObject",
    "com.google.gson.JsonPrimitive",
